WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.190
- [Narrator] This is what
Lego products looked like

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.453
in the 1980s.

00:00:04.415 --> 00:00:05.427
♪ Lego maniac ♪

00:00:05.427 --> 00:00:07.666
And this is a Lego product now

00:00:07.666 --> 00:00:09.430
♪ Everything is awesome ♪

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:13.140
That's because the company has
become more than just blocks.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.350
- They have video games,
movies, theme parks,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.350
all these activities which
ultimately reinforce the core,

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.780
which is the sale of Lego sets.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.370
- [Narrator] All that
content helped it become

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.230
the world's largest toy maker,

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.990
raking in billions of dollars every year.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.930
Here's how the company uses
licensing deals in media

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:35.160
to expand its customer base
and build its content empire.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.670
This is the Economics of Lego.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.740
- Lego is 90 years old.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.230
It was founded in Denmark in 1932

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.630
and initially it was a
company that made wooden toys,

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:49.590
but then in the 1950s, it
launched its trademark product,

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.650
the one we all know now,
the plastic Lego brick.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.710
- [Narrator] Since then, Lego
has be out Hasbro and Mattel

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:58.290
to become the biggest toy brand worldwide.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.480
In the first six months of 2022,

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.510
the company's revenue hit
27 billion Danish Kroner,

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:08.510
or about $3.47 billion, up 17% from 2021.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.890
And it's anticipating growing demand,

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:13.830
so much so that the company's
building two new factories

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.210
in the US and Vietnam.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:17.250
Lego has made the bricks
the building blocks

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.540
of its business.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.730
- Lego is still essentially a toy company.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:21.600
What they always say

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.590
is their core is still to make
the plastic bricks for kids,

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:27.990
but, of course, they do now
do a lot more than that.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.450
- [Narrator] Some of Lego's
first moves into content

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.933
started in the 1990s.

00:01:31.933 --> 00:01:33.600
- [Lego Character] The
island is right behind us!

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.340
- [Narrator] When the
company's sales slumped.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.230
It was trying everything,

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.290
from new toys to
electronics to theme parks.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.300
- [Announcer] Can you find the power?

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.133
Bionicle!

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:45.810
- Bionicles came along in the early 2000s,

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:46.643
and that was a time

00:01:46.643 --> 00:01:48.750
when the Lego brand was actually in danger

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.190
of becoming a little bit stale.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:51.390
- [Narrator] The Bionicle franchise

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:53.220
featured buildable action figures

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.230
and multi-platform storytelling.

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:58.200
- [Announcer] Agile,
determined, unstoppable.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.390
- [Narrator] The franchise
built a content universe

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.420
through comics, books,
movies, and video games.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.920
The bet proved successful.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:09.450
In 2003, when the toy maker
saw 26% loss in net sales,

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.730
Bionicle was its best selling line.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.920
- And it really revitalized the brand

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:17.430
and showed them a way that
they could engage audiences

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.260
with different types of content,

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:22.620
with cartoons, movies, comics.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.630
- [Narrator] And it wasn't
just original stories.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.750
Lego released its first sets
based off of license material

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.270
in 1999, "Star Wars".

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.640
In 2005, it brought that into content

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:35.190
with a five minute short
called "Revenge of the Brick"

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:37.023
that aired on Cartoon Network.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.920
- It was a twist, of course,
on the "Revenge of the Sith",

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.890
which was the "Star Wars" movie,
which came out at the time.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:47.100
That really paved the way
for the content partnerships

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.230
which we've seen in subsequent years.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.420
- [Narrator] That Lego twist
has since been put to use

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.310
on all sorts of franchises,

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.980
like "Batman", "Marvel",
and "Jurassic World".

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.480
- Really, we are now used to seeing

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.220
not just the basic Lego kits,

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.350
but Lego "Star Wars" kits and so on.

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:04.110
That's really an integral
part of what Lego does now.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:08.370
So, really, the content has
changed Lego's identity.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:11.730
We think of it as part of
these popular franchises

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.620
which we all know, like "Marvel".

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.900
- [Narrator] And licensed
material was on full display

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:19.500
on the company's smash hit,
2014's "The Lego Movie",

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.920
which grossed over $450 million worldwide.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.440
It held the top spot in the US box office

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.420
for three weeks after its release.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.220
- [Vitruvius] Superman,
Wonder Woman, the Mermaid,

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:33.180
Michelangelo, and the 2002 NBA All Stars.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.780
- The goal of "The Lego
Movie" was to market Lego

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:37.920
to a wider audience.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.080
I think it was a lot more
successful than anyone imagined.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.690
It was a very successful
movie in its own right,

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:44.130
a big hit at the box office.

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:46.890
That laid the template for a
lot of the content creation

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.210
that Lego has done since then.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:49.860
- [Narrator] Lego and
Warner Brothers released

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.460
three more feature films,
the latest in 2019.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.560
None earned as much as the first.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.020
- Of course, there is a
risk of oversaturation.

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:00.690
Lego doesn't want to do too much,

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.550
but I think they're still very much

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.860
at the stage of growing
in a lot of markets.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.390
- [Narrator] Content
has helped the toy maker

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.520
break into new places like China,

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.500
where Lego is growing its presence.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:14.388
Of the 66 new stores it opened
in the first half of 2022,

00:04:14.388 --> 00:04:16.230
46 of those were in China.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:20.550
Almost 42% of the company's
833 locations are there.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:23.700
Movies and games assist in
raising awareness of the brand.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.440
- The main challenge Lego has faced

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:26.850
in new markets like China

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.080
is that the grownups, the parents,

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.760
just don't really know about Lego.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.160
They don't have Lego in
their own backgrounds

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.130
like a lot of grownups
in the US and Europe do.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:37.560
- [Narrator] And using licensed
material in that content

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.450
also helps reach more audiences.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:41.610
- Being part of these popular franchises,

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:44.040
like "The Avengers", for example,

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:47.580
is a great way for Lego to reach out

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.310
to all kinds of different generations,

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.960
people across the world,

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.060
people who don't
necessarily even know Lego.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.380
- [Narrator] Content is also a way

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:57.480
for it to appeal to its adult fans,

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.180
as the brand has been trying
to do in recent years.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:01.800
- [Announcer] Find your Flow.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.570
Build with Lego Bricks.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:06.000
- [Narrator] Reality TV show
"Lego Masters", for example,

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.730
features adults building extreme creations

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:11.280
out of the titular plastic bricks.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.890
- The original Lego fans
took to Lego as kids

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:14.910
and they're now grown up

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:18.180
and a lot of those people
are still very keen on Lego

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.190
and I think Lego very smartly realized

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:24.240
that a lot of those people
would be willing to buy kits

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:26.610
that are are pretty
complex, pretty expensive,

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:29.010
and are designed
specifically for grownups.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.300
- [Narrator] The company has its eye set

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.460
beyond just the two-dimensional screen.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:35.460
Last April, Lego and Epic
Games announced a partnership

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:38.160
to build a digital
experience in the Metaverse.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.330
- All of this content,

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.030
certainly in the company's
current thinking,

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:43.530
the movies, the games,

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:46.530
that all is there to
support the core product,

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:48.870
which is the same as it
has been for decades,

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.567
the plastic brick.

00:05:50.567 --> 00:05:53.234
(playful music)

